                <pb facs="0696" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg606"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.825/67: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-12-26T16:00:00-05:00">December 26, 1934—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>395. Your 588, December 20, 3 p.m. in regard to pilotage regulations. The
                    Department concurs in the recommendations contained in paragraph 6 of the
                    above-mentioned telegram and authorizes the Legation to take action accordingly.
                    The procedure suggested in the last sentence of your telegram is approved.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
